sec.p:
The similarity between the two subtracted density plots was evaluated by calculating the 2D cross-correlation C using the following equation
C=∑m=1M∑n=1NX(m,n)Y(m,n)∑m=1M∑n=1NX(m,n)X(m,n)∑m=1M∑n=1NY(m,n)Y(m,n) \begin{document}$$\displaystyle C=\frac{\sum_{m=1}^{M} \sum_{n=1}^{N} X(m, n) Y(m, n)}{\sqrt{\sum_{m=1}^{M} \sum_{n=1}^{N} X(m, n) X(m, n)} \sqrt{\sum_{m=1}^{M} \sum_{n=1}^{N} Y(m, n) Y(m, n)}}$$\end{document}
where X and Y correspond to the two subtracted density matrices. The 11 different subtracted density plots shown in Figure 2 were clustered using the MATLAB function “linkage,” and the average distance between all pairs of elements in the two samples was calculated using the cluster algorithm.
